{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522347-how-likely-would-the-3rd-generation-would-care-about-their-clans","id":1522347,"title":"How likely would the 3rd generation would care about their clans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-10T10:43:55-07:00","id":1522347,"title":"How likely would the 3rd generation would care about their clans?","content":"Just an interesting notion on how much time they would spend keeping tabs on their respective clans. Outside of maybe feeling some emotional ties to there direct childer or eldest grand childer and wanting to know if they are doing well or find lore that might help with their transcending there curses.<br /> <br /> I just can\u2019t see them caring enough about members very far removed from them outside of some strange curiosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T11:18:00-07:00","id":1522349,"title":"","content":"I think they would only see them as pawns or snacks, after all they have already distanced themselves so much from humanity or anything else that they no longer see anything as an equal, even their desire to ascend and become almost deities is just a goal that they can have, because without it they no longer have a reason to &quot;live&quot;, much like the other clans and their Jyhad games to be frank. Of course there are exceptions, but you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T11:49:30-07:00","id":1522351,"title":"","content":"I certainly do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T12:22:14-07:00","id":1522352,"title":"","content":"Haqim - was by all accounts very hands-on with his Clan and actively involved in the early structuring. Of course, he eventually got tired of it, so maybe Ur-Shulgi's purge is actually him putting his foot down after all those years. Then again maybe not. A confrontation between Ur-Shulgi and Haqim would have been fun.<br /> <br /> Troile - probably not. They don't strike me as the kind of person who put their personal needs behind those of others, even before they spent millennia in torpor under salted earth seeped in Baali rituals.<br /> <br /> Ilyes - if still around, hates his Clan and wants them destroyed.<br /> <br /> Sutekh - bwahaha no.<br /> <br /> Ennoia - couldn't care less. A member of her own Clan walking over the wrong plot of land is as good a snack as any.<br /> <br /> Augustus - would sacrifice all of his own Clan without hesitation if it made him more powerful. He's willing to sacrifice the whole damn world for it.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius - evidently cared a lot. So much so he put all the progeny that did not comply with his vision into a big jar and put a lid on it.<br /> <br /> [Lasombra] - would ditch his Clan if his Clan didn't ditch him first.<br /> <br /> Malkav - in a weird way, does care. Whether that is a good thing or a bad thing is questionable, but if he continues to exist within the Clan as the Madness Network it does not seem to be entirely self-serving (and can not be if he wants to continue that way)<br /> <br /> Absimiliard - hates his Clan and wants them destroyed.<br /> <br /> Zapathasura - too hungry to care.<br /> <br /> Arikel - there is a lot of Mother-Goddess/protector-deity in their lore, so there is a decent chance they would try to actively run their Clan instead of simply eating it. Not that I imagine that anything less but cruel, but they at least seem to derive some pleasure from social interactions.<br /> <br /> Tremere - has literally built his Clan as a support structure for himself, only to have it rug-pulled from under his feet. I'm sure he would love to have it back.<br /> <br /> [Tzimisce] - uses its Clan as proxy structure for itself. Probably cares as much about them as a commuter about the subway network. Although it has shown some interest in individual members, but more as play things.<br /> <br /> [Ventrue] - no idea.<br /> <br /> and finally<br /> <br /> Saulot (The Wise) - deeply cares for all his childer and will lead them to transcendence.<br /> <br /> Saulot (The Horrible) - created new bloodlines as metaphysical experiments and then utterly ignored them when they did not turn out as he thought they should. Probably would create a dozen more in the face of Gehenna in hopes something sticks, and then forget about them, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[