level instead of physical and he IS his Clan... or like the Borg<br /> Every Malkav is inside the Hive Mind and individually not important - and if one dies, just lives on as a Voice in the Choir<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1522347-how-likely-would-the-3rd-generation-would-care-about-their-clans?p=1522352#post1522352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zapathasura - too hungry to care.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Before that, he not really cared about them either<br /> Embraced his Childrens to be leaders of his clan-army and got really upset when most of them eventually got tired and left him<br /> They cared as much about them as an archer about the arrows in the quiver; made sure to be plenty around to be used, and notices when there are to few<br /> But thats it<br /> <br /> <br /> All the Antediluvians had a goal or agenda<br /> Ishtar and Arikel are weird excepetions, because they only wanted to survive and chill with their current lovers and not really bothered their lines or used them for anything... just time to time Embraced then got bored and moved on and from those Childrens a Clan blossomed<br /> Maybe thats why the Toreador was/is called\u200b the Clan of the Blossom<br /> <br /> Veddartha is another &quot;wild card&quot;<br /> Except the fact he Embraced time to time (even after his &quot;death&quot;\u200b) never really bothered his Clan or used them. The structure and traditions and everything came from Artemis Orthia basically and other Methuselah\u200bs<br /> I guess back in the First City Caine scared him so much - if the Ventrue Clanbook story is true - with the tales of the Secret Masters he basically became the first and only &quot;real&quot; Inconnu and dissapeared from the scene and removed himslef from the Jyhad even before it started - But embraced a few, just in case time to time to have a few pieces on the board to keep an eye on the world and the Masters' signs of activity; they are his Monitors, if you will, but they don' even know it, thus they are perfect for the job; even if captured they couldn't reveal something they don't even know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}